# JSDoc types (required when generating code)

The project uses [jsconfig.json](mdc:jsconfig.json) with `allowJs` + `checkJs` for editor type checking. **Every change that adds or edits exported functions, hooks, or components in `app/` must include correct JSDoc** — not only the new code, but also fix typings on adjacent exports you touch.

Tracker for area-by-area cleanup: [docs/jsdoc-type-review.md](mdc:docs/jsdoc-type-review.md).

## When to add JSDoc

- New or changed **exported** functions and methods
- New or changed **React components** (props)
- New or changed **custom hooks** (params + return type)
- New **`@typedef`** shapes reused across a module
- Generic helpers — use `@template`

Do not leave new exports with implicit `any` parameters.

## Patterns (match nearby files)

**Utility / core / libs function**

```js
/**
 * @param {Request} request
 * @param {string} key
 * @returns {string | null}
 */
export function getCookieValue(request, key) { /* ... */ }
```

**Generic helper**

```js
/**
 * @template T
 * @param {string} key
 * @param {() => Promise<T>} refresh
 * @returns {Promise<T>}
 */
export async function getCachedResult(key, refresh) { /* ... */ }
```

**Shared object shape**

```js
/** @typedef {{ limit: number, windowMs: number }} RateLimitConfig */
```

**React component props** (see `app/components/admin/`)

```js
/**
 * @param {Object} props
 * @param {string} props.title
 * @param {(id: string) => void} props.onSelect
 */
export function MyComponent({ title, onSelect }) { /* ... */ }
```

**Prisma / external types**

```js
/** @typedef {import('#/generated/prisma/client').Order} Order */
```

## Typing hygiene

- `@returns` must match actual return values (`null` vs `undefined` — normalize or document accurately).
- Prefer concrete types over `any`; use `unknown` for unvalidated input, then narrow.
- Use `Request`, `Headers`, `Response` for Web API parameters.
- Do not add `// @ts-ignore` or `// @ts-expect-error` unless unavoidable — fix the types instead.
- When editing a file, bring incomplete JSDoc on touched exports up to the same standard.

## Validation

When you add or change typed exports, run a quick check on touched files:

```bash
npx -p typescript tsc --noEmit --allowJs --checkJs --strict \
  --module preserve --moduleResolution bundler --target es2020 --jsx react-jsx \
  "path/to/changed-file.js"
```
